      Save as <code>demo.c</code>, compile with <code>gcc -Wall -o demo demo.c</code>, run with <code>./demo</code>. The absolute addresses will differ each run because of address-space-layout randomisation, but the relative jumps of 4 bytes vs 20 bytes are always the same. That's the type system doing its job.
